  "DMs in shell + topic-match group-chat-proposals + historical-match
  doc-suggestions" gap. Suggestions are first-class durable records
  (suggestions table) so accept/decline/mute is auditable. Three suggestion
  kinds initially: group-chat-proposal, prior-art-doc, claim-overlap-headsup,
  salvage-candidate. The pd:dispatch-coord-2026-05-20 channel that got
  created manually after the fact would have been auto-proposed when the
  three involved agents' classifications converged on the dispatch verb.

0040 — PD-Encompassing Shell:
  Generalizes pd-shim from git-only (ADR-0037) to arbitrary tools via
  PATH-prepended symlinks. Per-session shim dir composes
  ~/.port-daddy/shims/<session-id>/ before $PATH. Each shim emits a
  tool.invoked event, routes verbs by mutation severity (read-only,
  local-mut, destructive, network), then exec's the real binary. Harness-
  agnostic because the observation boundary is the OS-process boundary,
  not the harness API. pd shell wraps this: composes the PATH, binds
  ambient session env, sources existing rc, prompt-loop polls pd attention.
  Operator's actual normal shell still works; pd shell is the
  session-scoped ergonomic wrapper.

Both ADRs explicitly compose with what's already there (pd attention,
lib/agent-inbox, lib/messaging, lib/activity, ADR-0037 git-shim, ADR-0030
talent-phonebook). Both flag the known ADR numbering collision pattern
from ADR-0037's §Phase A scope note — 0039/0040 picked on the assumption
that 0036 is bosun (PR #130 in-flight) and remain TBD until the
single-writer ADR registry lands.


