+# 0039. Suggestibility Layer — Topical Match Coaching for Active Agents
+
+## Status
+
+Draft (proposed 2026-05-22).
+
+Numbering risk: the ADR cluster has a known collision pattern (three `0028-*.md`
+files already coexist, see ADR-0037 §Phase A scope note). This ADR picks `0039`
+on the assumption that `0036` belongs to PR #130 (bosun) and remains TBD until
+the single-writer ADR registry lands.
+
+## Context
+
+`pd attention` (lib/attention.ts, landed via PR #169) aggregates the two
+addressed-at-you surfaces — personal inbox and subscribed channels — into one
+call wired into harness SessionStart hooks. That closes the *reactive* loop:
+when another agent has DM'd you, you'll see it.
+
+The product gap the operator named on 2026-05-22:
+
+> I want a suggestibility layer for agents. I want DMs to come into their
+> shell. I want little notifications like "hey it looks like you're working on
+> $feature, so are agents-X and agents-Y, shall I create an ad hoc group chat
+> for you three? ... hey, you're building a grammar for 3D ships based on
+> fleet agents, we did this before, check out these docs."
+
+DMs are the trivial case — `pd attention` already delivers them. The
+non-trivial cases:
+
+1. **Topic-match group-chat suggestion.** Three agents are independently
+   working on what is materially the same surface. The substrate sees this
+   (file claims overlap, session purposes look similar, recent edits cluster).
+   Today nobody tells the agents. On 2026-05-19 three agents on
+   `pd:dispatch-coord-2026-05-20` discovered the overlap by accident — the
+   channel was created manually after the fact, not auto-proposed.
+
+2. **Historical-match doc suggestion.** An agent is building a grammar for
+   3D-ship fleet-agent specs. We have episodic memory, skill index,
+   cartographer surface finder, and 50+ ADRs that may already cover prior art.
+   Nobody surfaces them to the agent unprompted.
+
+Both cases are *coaching*, not coordination. The difference: coordination is
+when another agent puts something in your inbox. Coaching is when the
+substrate itself notices something you'd want to know.
+
+What we have today:
+
+| Capability | Module | Used today as |
+|---|---|---|
+| Activity firehose | lib/activity.ts | History log; `/activity/subscribe` SSE |
+| Personal inbox | lib/agent-inbox.ts | DM delivery |
+| Channel broker | lib/messaging.ts | Pub/sub coordination |
+| Aggregator | lib/attention.ts | Harness SessionStart hook |
+| Episodic memory | lib/episodic-memory.ts | Past-session lookup |
+| Cartographer surface finder | lib/spider.ts + ADR-0031 | Surface→feature index |
+| Skill index | skill-search service | Skill → past artifact retrieval |
+| File claims | lib/sessions.ts | Per-region ownership |
+| Soft-claim broadcast | ADR-0037 §Layer 1 | git-shim overlap warnings |
+
+What's missing is the layer that *runs the inference* (am I working on the
+same thing as someone else? is there prior art for this?) and *queues the
+output* into a place `pd attention` already reads from.
+
+## Decision
+
+Three new primitives, all composable with the existing substrate.
+
+### Primitive 1 — Topical classifier (`lib/agent-context-classifier.ts`)
+
+An async Haiku call (cost-tier `low`, resolved via `lib/llm-backend-resolver.ts`
+with `actor: 'context-classifier'`) that runs every 60–90s per active agent.
+
+Input fingerprint for each call:
+
+- Session purpose + identity
+- Last 20 entries from `pd notes` for the session
+- Currently claimed file regions (lib/sessions.ts)
+- Last 20 entries from `/activity/subscribe` filtered to this session's agent
+- Last 10 git diff hunks via `git diff origin/main...HEAD --stat`
+
+Output (strict JSON, validated):
+
+```typescript
+interface ClassifierOutput {
+  agentId: string;
+  topicTag: string;            // free-form, ~3-8 words, e.g. "cockpit dispatch wiring"
+  topicEmbedding: number[];    // for cross-agent similarity
+  confidence: number;          // 0..1
+  surfaceClaims: string[];     // e.g. ["routes/cockpit.ts", "lib/dispatch.ts"]
+  generatedAt: number;
+}
+```
+
+Stored as tuples on a `agent:context` stream so the broker can read recent
+classifications across all agents in one fold.
+
+### Primitive 2 — Suggestion broker (`lib/suggestion-broker.ts`)
+
+Periodic (every 30–60s) scan over the latest classifier outputs. For each
+active agent, computes candidate suggestions:
+
+| Suggestion kind | Trigger | Composes with |
+|---|---|---|
+| `group-chat-proposal` | ≥2 other agents with topicEmbedding cosine > 0.85 and overlapping `surfaceClaims` | `pd msg publish` to create channel; `pd attention --subscribe` for each invitee |
+| `prior-art-doc` | topicEmbedding nearest-neighbor against ADR + skill + episodic-memory indices crosses threshold | Returns artifact paths + cosine score |
+| `claim-overlap-headsup` | This agent claimed a region that another active agent already claimed (today this is ADR-0037 §soft-claim; we promote it from inline shim warning to durable suggestion) | Soft-claim broadcast |
+| `salvage-candidate` | An idle session with dead-codex notes is sitting on claims this agent needs | `pd salvage` |
+
+Each candidate runs through:
+
+1. **Confidence floor**: default 0.85 (operator-configurable per kind).
+2. **Cooldown**: `(agentId, kind, payloadHash)` cooldown table; default 4h
+   per-tuple — declining a group-chat proposal mutes the exact triplet for
+   that window.
+3. **Budget**: hard cap of N suggestions per agent per hour (default 6).
+   Composes with existing fleet budget primitives (lib/budget-guard.ts).
+4. **Mute list**: per-agent + per-kind explicit mutes
+   (`pd attention --mute kind:group-chat-proposal --until +24h`).
+
+Accepted suggestions become first-class durable records:
+
+```sql
+CREATE TABLE suggestions (
+  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
+  agent_id TEXT NOT NULL,
+  kind TEXT NOT NULL,
+  payload TEXT NOT NULL,           -- JSON
+  confidence REAL NOT NULL,
+  status TEXT NOT NULL,            -- pending|accepted|declined|expired|muted
+  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,
+  acted_on_at INTEGER,
+  muted_until INTEGER
+);
+CREATE INDEX idx_suggestions_pending ON suggestions(agent_id, status, created_at DESC)
+  WHERE status = 'pending';
+```
+
+### Primitive 3 — Delivery via `pd attention`
+
+No new delivery channel. The broker writes accepted candidates into the
+target agent's inbox via lib/agent-inbox.ts with `type: 'suggestion'` and a
+structured payload. `pd attention` already returns these, the harness already
+pins them into the next-turn prompt, and the agent can respond with:
+
+```
+pd suggestion accept <id>        # acts on the suggestion (creates channel, opens doc, etc.)
+pd suggestion decline <id>       # declines and primes the cooldown
+pd suggestion mute kind:<kind> --until +Nh
+```
+
+The `accept` action dispatches based on `kind`:
+
+- `group-chat-proposal` → `pd channel create` + `pd attention --subscribe` for each invitee
+- `prior-art-doc` → emit a `pd attention` follow-up with the artifact text inlined
+- `claim-overlap-headsup` → emit a `pd inbox send` to the other claim-holder
+- `salvage-candidate` → `pd salvage --session <id>` with notes
+
+## What this unlocks
+
+- **The `pd:dispatch-coord-2026-05-20` channel** would have been auto-proposed
+  the moment the three involved agents' classifications converged on
+  `dispatch verb`. The channel still gets created manually OR via accepted
+  suggestion — same outcome, just earlier and without operator
+  intervention.
+
+- **Cross-session prior-art discovery.** An agent starting work on something
+  that overlaps with an existing skill or past episodic-memory session gets
+  prompted before it duplicates work. Today the operator's memory and the
+  agent's classifier are the only two paths; this makes it ambient.
+
+- **Audit and tuning.** `suggestions` table is queryable: which kinds get
+  accepted vs declined? Operator can quiet whole categories
+  (`pd attention --mute kind:prior-art-doc`) without code changes.
+
+## Risks
+
+1. **Noise spam destroys the channel.** Mitigations: confidence floor 0.85
+   (ramp up from telemetry), per-triplet cooldown, hard budget, per-agent
+   mute, operator-visible audit table. The "log every suggestion that fired,
+   even ones we suppressed" is critical for tuning.
+
+2. **Classifier hallucination.** A misclassified topic tag produces a
+   misdirected group chat proposal. Mitigation: classifier output schema is
+   strict JSON; mismatched embeddings get caught by the cosine threshold;
+   accept-rate per agent is monitored — if any agent's classifier output
+   produces <30% accept rate over its last 50 suggestions, that classifier
+   instance is paused and the operator is pinged.
+
+3. **Cost.** Haiku at 60–90s cadence per active agent. Assume 5 active
+   agents × $0.001/call × 40 calls/h = $0.20/h. Hard cap via the existing
+   budget-guard. Sleep classifier when session is idle (no shim events in
+   last 5 min).
+
+4. **Privacy / scope.** Cross-agent classifier reads see other sessions'
+   purposes + claims. Acceptable today (single-operator), needs revisit when
+   multi-operator landscape is real (cross-operator embedding scoping).
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Should `pd attention` learn a `kind:suggestion` filter to let agents
+  opt-out of suggestions while staying on inbox + channels? Likely yes,
+  ship behind `--no-suggestions` flag.
+- The classifier's prompt template needs hardening against prompt injection
+  via session notes / commit messages. Treat session notes as untrusted
+  user input.
+- Embedding model choice: local (cheap, faster) vs Cohere/OpenAI
+  (better quality, costlier). Probably local for the cross-agent similarity
+  hot path, remote for the prior-art retrieval where quality matters more.
+
+## Migration
+
+Layer 1 (classifier): purely additive new tuple stream.
+Layer 2 (broker): purely additive new SQL table.
+Layer 3 (delivery): uses existing `pd attention` + inbox surface; new CLI
+verb `pd suggestion {accept,decline,mute}` to ship alongside.
+
+No breaking changes to any existing surface. Suggestions are off by default
+on existing fleets; an opt-in `pd-fleet.yml` `suggestions: { enabled: true }`
+turns them on.
+
+## Composes with
+
+- ADR-0037 — soft-claim broadcasts are the Layer-1 instance of this pattern;
+  ADR-0039 generalizes to non-git tools and adds confidence + persistence.
+- ADR-0030 — talent phonebook is the same "find who's relevant" computation
+  applied to a different output channel (DMs instead of suggestions).
+- ADR-0040 (PD-encompassing shell, this batch) — provides the in-shell
+  delivery surface for human operators driving sessions interactively.
